A||||15||sluppy123||Crashed Fiero Pic||||13||
Z||000000||sluppy123||12-13-1999||09:37 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/fierogt321/myhomepage/good%20small%20crashed%20fiero.jpg">  <P>This picture was in my local newspaper so I thought I would share it with everybody.<BR>I think it's either a 86' or 87' SE. A couple was driving down the Interstate at 65-75 MPH when the driver lost control and ran head-on into a concrete base of a road sign. The woman driver was ejected out the driver's door and the passenger was pinned in the vehicle. Neither passenger was wearing a seat belt and both were critically injured. I think they are luckly to be alive, the force was so great it looks like it bent the frame where the cradle bolts to the frame.<P>-Brian<P><p>[This message has been edited by sluppy123 (edited 12-13-1999).]||||reg||13
Z||000001||87GT||12-13-1999||10:15 PM||||I dont think I have ever seen a fiero in that bad of a wreck.  I cant believe they werent killed at the scene.  I hope all goes well for them.  It does make me feel better about Fiero safety though.  wow||||reg||1
Z||000002||fiero56||12-13-1999||10:24 PM||||I feel bad for them, but they'd get a lot more sympathy from me if they were wearing their seatbelts.  I can't even move the car in the driveway without my seatbelt on, just feels too weird.  Everyone I drive <B> has </B> to wear a seatbelt or the car doesn't move. It one of my rules. A seatbelt is just common sense.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaRkLoRD||12-13-1999||10:42 PM||||I agree completely about the seatbelt comments.. I've always worn a seatbelt and I always will. a couple times I haven't, but that's just backing the car halfway out of the driveway and then driving it back into the center to wash it.. <P>On a related matter.. who else has seen the movie Demolition Man? The crash system in the police car is awesome. if the car crashes, the interior fills with rapidly expanding foam. like having an airbag all around you. once the car stops moving, or maybe right away, the foam starts disintegrating or breaking apart into little bits of styrofoam "popcorn".<BR>I think that would be a really cool system if it could be built.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||12-13-1999||11:08 PM||||Demolition man is a great movie.  It's been a few years since I last saw it, so I don't remember the foam part, but I do remember the taco bell part <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">. Too bad there's no Fieros in it.||||reg||1
Z||000005||fierospeeder||12-14-1999||12:26 AM||||theres a website someplace showing couple of fiero crashes and the passengers survived, proving that the fiero has a great safety design.  A lot of people say its a deathtrap just because the car is small but its just their uh ignorance.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DJRice||12-14-1999||08:37 AM||||So do the owners of that car want to sell the wing and sail panels?<P>Well Im kinda halfway joking but they look to have survived OK.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Monkeyman||12-14-1999||11:13 AM||||DJRice beat me to it, but you might want to see which junkyard got the car and salvage as many good parts as you can before someone else thinks of it.  (I assume these weren't close friends or anything.  In which case, greive for a few days, then hit the boneyard.  I know...I'm a callous, unfeeling bastard.)||||reg||1
Z||000008||batboy||12-14-1999||08:28 PM||||Well, I hate to see anyone get hurt in an accident, including Fieros. I've seen several Fieros in the salvage yards that had no business being there. But, regardless, I'd like to think of picking those junk Fieros' bones clean as <B><I>recycling</I></B>. Consider them as organ donors, so that other Fieros may live. I talked to a guy in Emporia once that I saw in a Fiero. We found out that both of our cars had parts on it from the same wrecked Fiero located at the Westside Auto Salvage Yard. Sometimes I wonder: just how many other Fieros have parts off that same junk car.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 12-14-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Racer 1||12-14-1999||11:35 PM||||I think the fiero in the picture has a "HOLLEY" sidescoop on it look at the picture close. And that wing on E-Bay is worth $150+..||||reg||6
Z||000010||Racer 1||12-15-1999||12:28 PM||||Oh yeah I dont think the engine caught on fire! ||||reg||1
Z||000011||dogtired||12-15-1999||02:43 PM||||YOU guys are AWFUL! YOU guys are MORBID!<BR>I wonder if there are any christmas presents in the trunk?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"><P>I hate to see anyone in a life threating situation, especially a car crash. HOPE they recover soon.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000012||Monkeyman||12-15-1999||03:57 PM||||Too bad it isn't an '88.  Then you could get the upgraded rear suspension, too.  We *are* terrible.  Wonder what condition the seats are in?||||reg||1
Z||000013||sluppy123||12-15-1999||05:31 PM||||Well I called around and finally found the car in a bone yard. The bad news is there isn't a exterior body panel that dosen't have a crack in it, the wing is split down the middle, decklid has a large hole in it. The interior looks like it was in good shape before the crash but now it's pretty much broken up,(both seats have some nice blood stains on them, I think I'll pass)<P>The only good parts I'm going to get is the "Holley" scoop and maybe the rear honeycomb wheels, the front one's both have flat spots.<P>-Brian||||reg||13
Z||000014||Monkeyman||12-16-1999||01:26 AM||||Are the seats in good shape other than the blood spots?  This is a serious question.  You can always recover the seats.  What about other misc parts?  Switches, gauges, etc may have survived intact.  What about the cradle or at least the suspension?  I suppose the brakes are trashed since they obviously couldn't stop in time.||||reg||5
Z||000015||sluppy123||12-16-1999||08:24 PM||||Monkeyman- The seats looked like the backs were bent forward with the firerwall pressing against them. As for the gauge pod there wasn't much left of any of the gauges or switches, the steering wheel took most of them out. The cradle might be in decent shape, the engine may have broken some mounts because it was in there crooked.<P>-Brian||||reg||1
